{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Itaï Ben Yaacov and Arthur Paul Pedersen, \"A proof of completeness for continuous first-order logic\", Journal of Symbolic Logic 75 (2010) 168–190 (arXiv:0903.4051). Framing: rigorous reconstruction/verification of continuous propositional and first-order syntax/semantics, Group 1 / Group 2 axioms, black-box theorems, and the completeness / approximated strong-completeness results, together with the selected decidability (Corollary 9.11) and compactness (Corollary 9.12) consequences. Project rule: no Lean `axiom` declarations. Itaï Ben Yaacov and Arthur Paul Pedersen did not participate in or endorse this formalization; they have not been contacted about it. Lean is written with AI-agent assistance under Lars Warren Ericson’s direction and review. Mathlib is the Lake dependency. Palomar registration pending; packaging follows the Challenge / Solution / comparator.json pattern. Deviation from the paper: Facts 4.2 and 4.3 (consistency iff satisfiability, Łukasiewicz and continuous propositional logic) needed the added premise that there is at least one propositional variable (`[Nonempty I]`). As literally stated they fail when there are no variables (the empty set is then satisfiable but inconsistent); this counterexample is proved in Lean (`LukPropForm.consistent_iff_satisfiable_fails_empty`, `CLPropForm.consistent_iff_satisfiable_fails_empty`).",
